5	 * \file src/transform/ascend_tail_mask_propagation.cc
6	 * \brief Propagate UB tail valid-regions and rewrite vector ops to tail-aware
7	 *        variants for the AscendC backend.
8	 *
9	 * After LowerTileOp, a GM->UB copy is lowered to
10	 *   call_extern("tl::ascend::copy_gm_to_ub<...>", src_ptr, dst_ptr,
11	 *               strideN, validRow, validCol, [physRow], physCol)
12	 * and the element-wise / reduce ops are plain tl.ascend_* calls whose `count`
13	 * argument spans the whole physical tile.
14	 *
15	 * This pass tracks, per UB data Var, the logical valid rectangle that was
16	 * loaded, propagates it through the UB data flow, and when an op touches a tail
17	 * buffer rewrites it to the internal tl.ascend_tail_* op (carrying the runtime
18	 * valid_row/valid_col/physical_col) so the codegen emits a tl::ascend::tail_*
19	 * helper that computes only over the valid region.
20	 *
21	 * Batch 1 rewrites: unary / binary / scalar(immediate) / reduce.
22	 * Batch 1 propagates-but-does-not-rewrite: cast / broadcast / copy_ub_to_ub
23	 * (they are per-lane or shape-only, so the full-tile path stays numerically
24	 * correct; the mask still flows through to a downstream reduce).
25	 */
